; All view ops
(constructor LogicalIndexMapApply (LogicalTensor IndexMap Shape) LogicalTensor)

; THE COMPOSITION CLOSURE. An index map is a lambda: the apply's out shape
; binds the coordinates, the entries are the body, the tag is the parent
; shape it reads. `(IndexMapCompose inner outer)` is the lambda for a view
; of a view, held CLOSED: first the outer map (the view's coordinates into
; the intermediate box; its tag is the intermediate shape), then the inner
; (the intermediate box into the parent; its tag is the parent shape). The
; composite's tag is the inner's. Its body is never written into the
; e-graph by the structural rule (rewrite.egg): beta reduction happens
; once, under `index-map-open-demand`, when the composite is unioned with
; its `IndexMapLit`; a kernel elected over a closed composite has its two
; literals composed in Rust after extraction (`index_expr::parse_index_map`).
; The structural rule composes LITERAL pairs only, so a closed composite
; never feeds another composition and a cyclic class holds at most one
; composite per literal pair.
(constructor IndexMapCompose (IndexMap IndexMap) IndexMap)
; The source-shape tag of any map: a literal's own child, a composite's
; inner's. :no-merge — a map with two tags is corrupt, and a composite
; opened to a literal of another tag collides here.
(function index-map-tag (IndexMap) Shape :no-merge)

; The relations of rewrite.egg, declared with the constructor so every op's
; rewrites can name them whatever the splice order.
; The identity-map fold.
(relation index-map-identity-suffix (IntExprList Shape))
; Opening a composite: the demand (a consumer demands a NAMED composite,
; never every composite of a class — on a cyclic class that would
; enumerate the powers of the map), the entry walk (the inner's entries
; substituted under the outer map, one `int-subst-of` row per entry), and
; the coordinate-only analysis under which a composite opens without
; demand.
(relation index-map-open-demand (IndexMap))
(relation composed-entries-demand (IntExprList IndexMap))
(relation composed-entries (IntExprList IndexMap IntExprList))
(relation coordinate-only-entries-demand (IntExprList))
(relation coordinate-only-entries (IntExprList))
(relation index-map-coordinate-only (IndexMap))
